pkix-chain-simple/src/lib.rs:456

  for ext in extensions.iter() {

Clippy (explicit_iter_loop) flags this as 'it is more concise to loop over references to containers instead of using explicit iteration methods'. The idiomatic form is:

  for ext in extensions {

The type of extensions is &Extensions (a slice reference), so iterating directly produces &Extension items, identical to .iter(). This is pure style with no functional difference, but it avoids the unnecessary method call.

Same pattern appears in multiple .iter() loops across pkix-path/src/lib.rs (lines 1310, 1318, 2105, 2155, etc.) — the fix is mechanical for all of them.
